   "unmapped": [
    "Super-arms come from an arbitrary combinatorial family M subset of {0,1}^K with |Z| <= d (paper's d = canonical m); family need not be a uniform matroid",
    "Learner has an exact oracle returning the max-weight super-arm, and the max-weight super-arm containing a given arm i",
    "Corruption at round t measured as the sum of the d largest absolute corruption components; adversary sees the reward vector before corrupting",
    "Reward range not explicitly stated; proofs use Chernoff-Hoeffding (bounded rewards assumed)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "After the environment generates the reward vector $R_t=[r_{t,i}]$, there is an adversary who can corrupt the reward after seeing $R_t$ ... For each $t$, we define the quantity $C_t=\\|\\tilde{R}_t-R_t\\|_{[d]}$ ... The total amount of corruption is defined as $C=\\sum_{t=1}^TC_t$."
  },
